    "detailed_description": "This is a puzzle game that integrates principles from both nonogram and genetics.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nGame features:<br />\r\n-Incorporates concepts from genetics such as genotype, phenotype, single gene inheritance, polygenic inheritance, and sex-linked inheritance into the game's -mechanics.<br />\r\n-Revamps the gameplay of nonogram to make it compatible with genetic mechanisms.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCommon Questions:<br />\r\nQ: Does the game require prior knowledge?<br />\r\nA: You need to have a basic understanding of high school genetics.<br />\r\nQ: How large is the game?<br />\r\nA: The game consists of 32 levels each for single gene inheritance, multi-gene inheritance, and sex-linked inheritance, totaling 96 levels. It takes 4-12 hours to complete all levels.<br />\r\nQ: Are the questions computer-generated?<br />\r\nA: Yes, but all levels have been manually selected, eliminating questions that rely too heavily on enumeration. Almost every step in each level can be logically deduced.<br />\r\nQ: Why are there settings like &quot;being your own offspring and parent&quot; and &quot;your parents being your offspring&quot;?<br />\r\nA: These settings add new reasoning clues for sex-linked inheritance questions.<br />\r\nQ: Any suggestions?<br />\r\nA: Make good use of the annotation button, especially the &quot;0&quot; and &quot;1&quot; buttons provided in sex-linked inheritance questions.",
